==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|sh|ota|بره|tr=bre}}, from {{bor|sh|el|μωρέ}}.

===Interjection===
{{sh-interjection}}

# {{lb|sh|Serbia|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|used to insist on or emphasize something being said or commanded, often also stressing the speaker’s perception of evidentness of the thing insisted on:}} [[man]], [[I say]], I’m [[tell]]ing you, can’t you [[see]]
# {{lb|sh|Serbia|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|used to insist on an answer to or emphasize a question:}} [[on earth]], [[the hell]]
#: {{ux|sh|Šta si '''bre''' to uradio!?|inline=1|What '''the hell''' did you just do!?}}
# {{lb|sh|Serbia|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|used to intensify a preceding interjection}}

====Usage notes====
When marking a statement or question as insistent, {{m|sh||bre}} is ordinarily found either immediately after the verb or at the end of the sentence. However, if an interjection or vocative is present, it can instead appear next to it, following an interjection and following or preceding a vocative. In [[wh-question]]s {{m|sh||bre}} can also follow the interrogative pronoun.

====Related terms====
* {{l|sh|bwe}}

===References===
* Jasmina Milićević (2012) “[http://www.ruslang.ru/doc/melchuk_festschrift2012/Milicevic.pdf ''Šta ustvari znači to bre?'' ‘What does this ''bre'' mean, actually?’ Defining Serbian interjection bre ≈ ‘I’m telling / asking you!’]”
* Mirjana Mišković-Luković, Mirjana N. Dedaić, and Vladimir Polomac (2015) “[https://www.academia.edu/15322511/The_meaning_and_interpretation_of_the_Serbian_discourse_marker_BRE_Journal_of_Pragmatics_87_2015_18_30 The meaning and interpretation of the Serbian discourse marker ''BRE'']” in ''Journal of Pragmatics'', vol. 87, pages 18–30

